<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armand-Emmanuel du Plessis, Duc de Richelieu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1766">1766</a>–<a href="/years/1822">1822</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Duke of Richelieu, Duc de Richelieu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Armand-Emmanuel du Plessis, Duc de Richelieu, was a French aristocrat who served <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> during the emigration as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odessa">Odessa</a>. Returning after 1814, he was prime minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> Restoration from 1815 to 1818 and from 1820 to 1821. He negotiated the payment of war indemnities and secured the end of the allied occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1818.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armand-emmanuel-du-plessis-duc-de-richelieu.jpg" alt="Armand-Emmanuel du Plessis, Duc de Richelieu" width="320" height="406" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Lawrence · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Armand_Emmanuel_Duke_of_Richelieu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
